.TH BURNSCANNER 1 "2026-08-05" "Burn Suite 1.0" "Burn Suite Manual"
.SH NAME
burnscanner \- automated network vulnerability scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo python3 ./burnscanner.py
.br
.B sudo burnscanner
.RI ( "if installed via " install.sh )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B burnscanner
discovers live hosts in a target network range, scans each for open
ports and service versions, queries the NVD CVE database for known
vulnerabilities in detected software, runs Nmap's vuln script suite
against each host, and optionally launches Metasploit against any
confirmed vulnerability. Results are written as a plain-text report to
.IR burn_report/ .
.PP
The tool is interactive: it prompts for a target, then runs unattended
through host discovery, port/service scanning, CVE lookup, and Nmap
vuln scripts. It will ask for explicit confirmation before attempting
any Metasploit exploit.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B nmap
Required. The tool exits immediately (code 2) if not found.
.TP
.B metasploit (msfconsole)
Optional \- only needed if you choose to attempt exploits.
.TP
.B python3\-requests
Required for CVE lookups against the NVD API.
.PP
Best results require root (SYN scans, OS detection, some NSE scripts).
Without root the tool still runs, in a degraded capacity.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B 1.
Enter a target IP or network range when prompted.
.br
Examples: \fB192.168.1.0/24\fR, \fB192.168.1.50\fR, \fB192.168.1.1\-50\fR
.TP
.B 2.
The tool pings the range to find live hosts, then for each host: scans
open ports/services, looks up CVEs for detected software versions
(cached per product+version to avoid redundant NVD queries within the
same scan), and runs Nmap's vuln script suite.
.TP
.B 3.
If any host has a confirmed vulnerability, you're asked whether to
search Metasploit and attempt an exploit. Nothing runs without your
explicit "yes" and your explicit module selection.
.TP
.B 4.
A \fB.txt\fR report is written to \fIburn_report/burnscan_<timestamp>.txt\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit the constants near the top of \fBburnscanner.py\fR:
.TP
.B REPORT_DIR
Where reports are written. Defaults to \fIburn_report/\fR next to the script.
.TP
.B SCAN_DIR
Scratch directory for intermediate Nmap XML output. Defaults to \fI/tmp/burnscan\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed normally.
.TP
.B 1
User cancelled or gave invalid input (e.g. no target entered).
.TP
.B 2
Environment/dependency problem (e.g. nmap not found).
.TP
.B 3
Target produced no usable data (e.g. no live hosts found).
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Every failure, skip, or empty result is logged to the console and to
the report's DIAGNOSTICS section as a \fBSCAN\-NNN\fR code. See
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
in the suite root for the full reference \- it explains which codes
represent a genuine "tested and clean" finding versus an incomplete
check that shouldn't be read as a security conclusion.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I burn_report/burnscan_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Generated report for each run.
.TP
.I /tmp/burnscan/
Scratch directory for Nmap XML output during a scan.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B FOR AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY.
Only scan networks and hosts you own or have explicit written
permission to test. Unauthorized scanning and exploitation is a
federal crime under the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA) and
equivalent laws worldwide. The Metasploit exploit step is gated
behind an explicit confirmation for this reason \- do not confirm it
without authorization.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR burncracker (1),
.BR burnrecon (1),
.BR burnweb (1),
.BR burnreport (1),
.BR burnsuite (7),
.BR nmap (1)
